Two rules are switched off deliberately:

  unicorn/no-new-array
    `new Array(n)` is intentional pre-allocation on hot paths (agent buckets,
    shelter tables, the loader's spatial grid). The suggested alternatives
    either allocate differently or are slower; every use is filled immediately.

  react/immutability (src/components/*.tsx only)
    The renderer deliberately mutates memoised caches and Three.js objects
    inside `useFrame`, which runs outside React's render phase. This is the
    architecture the simulation requires: 2,900 agents and 460 buildings are
    updated by writing into pre-allocated arrays and instance matrices, never
    through React state. The rule cannot tell `useFrame` from a render body.
